@startuml

salt
{
  <b>PUBLISH: USD IRS (approved candidates)</b> | [ Back to curves ]
  --
  {#
    Approval | Value
    Request | 8f1c... (marketdata.curve_publish)
    State | approved
    Approvals | 1 of 1
    Approved by | b.approver at 2026-10-06 16:31
    Reason | Today's USD curve, reviewed against the quotes
  }
  --
  {#
    Approved set | Point | Value | Approved
    . | tenor=1M | 0.04125 | yes
    . | tenor=3M | 0.04180 | yes
    . | tenor=1Y | 0.04095 | yes
    . | tenor=5Y | 0.04210 | yes
  }
  --
  {
    Published by | "a.trader (signed in)"
    Publish as of | "2026-10-06 16:00"
    [ Publish approved set ]
  }
  With approvals_required = 0 the raise publishes at once; no such path exists.
  --
  {#
    After publish | Consumer | Sees
    . | Pricing | published curve from 2026-10-06 16:00
    . | Reporting | published curve from 2026-10-06 16:00
  }
  Nothing marks a curve published; readers take the latest ticks.
  --
  {#
    Consumers told | Consumer | Notice | Sent
    . | (no notification kind) | - | no
  }
}

@enduml
